    },
    {
      "t": 121.56,
      "text": "arithmetic sequence.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 123.0,
      "text": "If I wanted to write it recursively, I",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 125.04,
      "text": "could say a sub one is equal to",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 128.48,
      "text": "negative five, and then each successive term for",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 132.66,
      "text": "a sub two and greater, so I could",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 134.74,
      "text": "say a sub n is equal to a",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 137.3,
      "text": "sub n minus one plus three.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 140.58,
      "text": "Each term is equal to the previous term",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 142.54,
      "text": "plus, not three, plus two.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 145.64,
      "text": "So this is for n greater than or",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 149.96,
      "text": "equal to two.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 151.06,
      "text": "So either of these are completely legitimate ways",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 155.34,
      "text": "of defining the arithmetic sequence that we have",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 159.8,
      "text": "here.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 160.2,
      "text": "We can either define it explicitly or we",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 162.64,
      "text": "could define it recursively.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 164.74,
      "text": "Let's look at this sequence.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 165.8,
      "text": "Is this one arithmetic?",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 168.48,
      "text": "Well, we're going from 100, we add seven,",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 172.22,
      "text": "107 to 114, we're adding seven, 114 to",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 175.8,
      "text": "121, we are adding seven.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 178.42,
      "text": "So this is indeed an arithmetic sequence, so",
