    },
    {
      "t": 312.5,
      "text": "a sub n is equal to a sub",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 314.74,
      "text": "n minus one, a given term is equal",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 317.06,
      "text": "to the previous term, plus d for n",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 320.34,
      "text": "greater than or equal to two.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 322.28,
      "text": "So once again, this is explicit, this is",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 324.3,
      "text": "a recursive way of defining it, and we",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 326.28,
      "text": "would just write with there.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 328.06,
      "text": "Now the last question I have is, is",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 329.6,
      "text": "this one right over here an arithmetic sequence?",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 332.38,
      "text": "Well, let's check it out.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 334.2,
      "text": "To start, we start one, then we add",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 336.54,
      "text": "two, then we add three, so this is",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 339.72,
      "text": "a immediate giveaway, this is not an arithmetic",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 341.22,
      "text": "sequence, now we are adding four, we're adding",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 343.56,
      "text": "a different amount every time.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 346.18,
      "text": "So how could we, so this first of",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 347.36,
      "text": "all, not, this is not arithmetic, this is",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 351.34,
      "text": "not an arithmetic sequence, but how could we",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 354.36,
      "text": "define this, since we're trying to define our",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 356.96,
      "text": "sequences?",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 358.38,
      "text": "So if we wanted to define it, if",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 360.44,
      "text": "we wanted to define it, let's say we",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 362.46,
      "text": "wanted to define it recursively, so this could",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 365.68,
      "text": "we could say this is equal to a",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 369.04,
      "text": "sub n, where n is starting at one,",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 371.94,
      "text": "and it's going to infinity, with, we'll say",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 376.62,
      "text": "our base case, a sub one is equal",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 378.86,
      "text": "to one, and then for n is two",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 381.72,
      "text": "or greater, a sub n is going to",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 383.96,
      "text": "be equal to what?",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 385.34,
      "text": "So a sub two is the previous term,",
